{"name":"Pipe Dream","hex":"#999d99","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pipe dream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A desire or idea which is unlikely to materialize, or a plan which is unlikely to work; a near impossibility. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipe_dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Opium pipe","blocks":[{"text":"An opium pipe is a pipe designed for the evaporation and inhalation of opium. True opium pipes allow for the opiate to be vaporized while being heated over a special oil lamp known as an opium lamp. It is thought that this manner of \"smoking\" opium began in the seventeenth century when a special pipe was developed that vaporized opium instead of burning it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/OPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG/330px-OPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opium_pipe"},{"title":"Pipe Dream (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Pipe Dream is the seventh musical by the team of Richard Rodgers and Oscar Hammerstein II; it premiered on Broadway on November 30, 1955. The work is based on John Steinbeck's novel Sweet Thursday—Steinbeck wrote the novel, a sequel to Cannery Row, in the hope of having it adapted into a musical. Set in Monterey, California, the musical tells the story of the romance between Doc, a marine biologist, and Suzy, who in the novel is a prostitute; her profession is only alluded to in the stage work. Pipe Dream was not an outright flop but was a financial disaster for Rodgers and Hammerstein."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Musical1955-PipeDream-OriginalPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pipe_Dream_(musical)"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/OPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG/500px-OPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/OPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG/500px-OPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Opium vaporization paraphernalia: An opium pipe, an opium lamp, spare pipe-bowls, and other implements lie arranged on a layout tray; a second opium pipe rests nearby.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOPIUM_LAYOUT.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Musical1955-PipeDream-OriginalPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Musical1955-PipeDream-OriginalPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMusical1955-PipeDream-OriginalPoster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Cy_Feuer.jpg/500px-Cy_Feuer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Cy_Feuer.jpg/500px-Cy_Feuer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cy Feuer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACy_Feuer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/John_Steinbeck_1962.jpg/330px-John_Steinbeck_1962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/John_Steinbeck_1962.jpg/330px-John_Steinbeck_1962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"John Steinbeck","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn_Steinbeck_1962.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Hammerstein.jpg/500px-Hammerstein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Hammerstein.jpg/500px-Hammerstein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oscar Hammerstein II","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHammerstein.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Doc_and_Hazel.jpg/500px-Doc_and_Hazel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Doc_and_Hazel.jpg/500px-Doc_and_Hazel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"William Johnson as Doc and Mike Kellin as Hazel, in Doc's lab","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADoc_and_Hazel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/All_at_once_you_love_her.jpg/500px-All_at_once_you_love_her.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/All_at_once_you_love_her.jpg/500px-All_at_once_you_love_her.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Suzy and Doc on their date. Jerry LaZarre is Esteban.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAll_at_once_you_love_her.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Happiest_house.jpg/500px-Happiest_house.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Happiest_house.jpg/1280px-Happiest_house.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Happiest_house.jpg/500px-Happiest_house.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Helen Traubel as Fauna and some of her \"girls\" in the Act 2 party scene","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHappiest_house.jpg"}],"sounds":{"pipe dream":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/91/En-au-pipe_dream.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/91/En-au-pipe_dream.ogg/En-au-pipe_dream.ogg.mp3"}]}}}